Theorem RL-31: neutral disjoint-Borrowed-parameter fact (CRITICAL)

  Preconditions:
    - RL-31 governs a backend-neutral `ParameterDisjointnessFact`, not LLVM
      metadata. Final realization freezes the fact once; VM, native, compiled
      WebAssembly, JIT, and LLVM consumers transport it without rerunning AIMS.
    - A pair is `proven` only when both parameters are Borrowed and BOTH
      disjointness facets hold:
        (a) every call site proves provenance disjointness;
        (b) type-level disjointness holds through `BurdenSpec.field_type`.
    - The provenance facet uses the full 8-clause sufficient condition:
        (1) both params Borrowed;
        (2) conjunction across ALL call sites;
        (3) root-set extraction filters `project_alias_sources` to variables
            with no upstream source;
        (4) disjoint root sets prove distinct source aggregates;
        (5) a fresh allocation contributes its own root;
        (6) untraceable arguments fail conservatively;
        (7) same-root fields are disjoint only when neither field path is a
            prefix of the other;
        (8) cross-function reasoning consumes the CALLERS' function-local
            `borrow_sources` and `project_alias_sources`, not IC-2/IC-3 alone.
    - RL-31 is the CRITICAL burden-prototype C5 closure and belongs to the
      Lean/checker cross-validation set.

  Soundness property:
    (P1) `ParameterDisjointnessFact.proven` iff the all-sites provenance facet
         and type facet both hold. Any failing/untraceable/overlapping site,
         or either facet alone, yields `notProven`.

    (P2) When a site proves disjointness, the two argument root sets have no
         common source aggregate. Same-root field proofs require the nested
         prefix-overlap test.

    (P3) The neutral fact is the authority. LLVM may project it to parameter
         `noalias` or alias-scope metadata only when a separate ABI/placement
         proof preserves the relation. An unproven fact or invalid placement
         forbids the target metadata. Other backends may use different physical
         encodings without changing the AIMS fact.

  Proof obligation:
    The refinement engine checks:
      - six provenance rows covering disjoint roots, fresh roots,
        untraceable failure, disjoint same-root fields, prefix overlap, and a
        non-Borrowed parameter;
      - the all-sites conjunction in both directions;
      - the dual-facet conjunction and type-only negative witness;
      - LLVM projection fidelity as a distinct target corollary.

    Lean 4 proves root-set soundness constructively, freezes
    `ParameterDisjointnessFact` from the dual facets, and separately proves
    `RL31_llvm_projection_fidelity` plus the unproven negative corollary.

